111 - It Took a Miracle
 / 
Key: G
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 111
Topic: God the Father - 

Verse 1:
[Am]My Father [D]is [B/D#]omnipotent, [Em]And [Am]that you can't deny;
[D7]A God of [G]might and miracles, 'Tis written in the sky.
[G]It took a [D7/A]miracle to put the stars in place;
[Am]It took [D7]a miracle to hang the world [G]in space.

Refrain:
[G]It took [Em]a miracle to put [Am]the stars in place;
[Am]It took a miracle to hang the world in space.
[Am]But when [D7]He saved my soul,
[D7]Cleansed and made [G]me whole,
[G]It took a miracle [Am]of [D7]love and grace!

Verse 2:
[Am]Though here [B/D#]His [Em]glory [Am]has been shown,
[D7]We [G]still can't fully see
[G]The wonders [D7/A]of His might, His throne;
[Am]'Till [D7]eternity.

Verse 3:
[Am]The Bible [Em]tells us of [Am]His power
[D7]And [G]wisdom all way through;
[G]And every [D7/A]little bird and flower
[Am]Are [D7]testimonies, [G]too.
